{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281118596347756068268d9d6n3jZLRNI","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_f161eb91399d4cfd8b565598d38bbae5","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"// Ah, the first time it worked but didn't throw because of asynchronous timing maybe or it was just successful.\n// Wait, let's write a script that creates a frame and text to verify.\n// Let's design the layout and components first!\n// We can instantiate the components:\n// 1. Button component:\n//    - \"6:7\" is component ID for Button variant \"Type=Primary, State=Default\"\n//    - Wait! Let's check what properties it has. We can duplicate/instantiate it using `figma.getNodeById(\"6:7\").createInstance()`.\n// 2. Text Field component:\n//    - \"6:23\" is variant \"Type=Text, State=Empty\". Let's instantiate it.\n// 3. Status Bar:\n//    - \"48:43\" is Status Bar.\n// 4. Home Indicator:\n//    - \"48:54\" is Home Indicator.\n// Let's verify if we can find these components programmatically and instantiate them.\n// Let's inspect the Button and Text Field properties and their internal structure so we know how to edit their text or set their state.\nconst buttonComp = figma.getNodeById(\"6:7\");\nconst tfComp = figma.getNodeById(\"6:23\");\nlet details = {};\nif (buttonComp) {\n  details.button = {\n    id: buttonComp.id,\n    type: buttonComp.type,\n    name: buttonComp.name,\n    children: buttonComp.children.map(c => ({ id: c.id, name: c.name, type: c.type }))\n  };\n}\nif (tfComp) {\n  details.textField = {\n    id: tfComp.id,\n    type: tfComp.type,\n    name: tfComp.name,\n    children: tfComp.children.map(c => ({ id: c.id, name: c.name, type: c.type }))\n  };\n}\nthrow new Error(\"DETAILS:\" + JSON.stringify(details, null, 2));\n","description":"Inspect children of the Button (\"6:7\") and Text Field (\"6:23\") components to see how to customize them.","fileKey":"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q"}