{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Error: CURRENT_PAGE:00 · Start Here 设计任务 (0:1)\n    at <anonymous> (PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:3:16)\n    at <eval> (PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:5:3)\n\nFigma Debug UUID: 40f14900-23b9-40b4-9600-ccc665862c29","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"call_d7955fb03fe04cff9c1b184940cca5ee"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885502f9-7195-4d21-a73d-fafd5215030c","uuid":"e66cfec1-4535-4d6a-ba39-455eec8d0eab","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:27:44.758Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"Error: Error: CURRENT_PAGE:00 · Start Here 设计任务 (0:1)\n    at <anonymous> (PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:3:16)\n    at <eval> (PLUGIN_1_SOURCE:5:3)\n\nFigma Debug UUID: 40f14900-23b9-40b4-9600-ccc665862c29","_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"40f14900-23b9-40b4-9600-ccc665862c29"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_d7955fb03fe04cff9c1b184940cca5ee","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281127451098849928268d9d6a99uQ3xm","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a3abbc1fb7ad4f949792a35eb73edf93","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"// Oh! The active page is still 00 · Start Here. Why did figma.setCurrentPageAsync not work?\n// Ah! In Figma Plugin API, you must set `figma.currentPage` directly as a property, e.g. `figma.currentPage = page`.\n// Wait, the skill says:\n// \"MUST use `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` to change pages. Setting figma.currentPage is not supported\"\n// Wait! Let's check why my `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)` didn't change it.\n// Oh, the script ended but perhaps the sandbox context didn't preserve the current page if it's running in separate sessions, OR we didn't await properly, or the page change is reset at the end of execution?\n// No, actually, when we execute a script, the page stays changed if it is committed. But wait! The tool says \"Code executed with no return value\" for the first script. Let's see if we should set the page and perform the operations IN THE SAME script!\n// Yes, in Figma, every tool call runs in a fresh plugin invocation, so any state changes like `figma.currentPage` might not persist across separate tool calls!\n// That is a crucial insight! We MUST do our page navigation AND design creation within the same script call, or at least perform the page setting at the beginning of EVERY script call that writes or edits.\n//\n// Let's design a master script that builds the frames inside 03 · Workspace.\n// First, let's write a script to set up the frames and structure.\n// Let's think about the designs.\n// Base viewport: 414 x 932\n//\n// Let's lay out the screens side by side.\n// We can position them in 3 rows or 1 row:\n// Row 1: 01_Splash, 02_Welcome, 03_Create_Account_Empty, 03_Create_Account_Filled, 03_Create_Account_Error (x spacing = 500)\n// Row 2: 04_Home, 05_My_Asset_Overlay, 06_Notification\n// Row 3: 07_Profile, 08_Contact_Info, 09_Bank_Account_Info\n//\n// Let's prepare a solid script that can create the screens one by one or in blocks, with precise elements, layouts, colors, typography.\n// Let's define the color palette:\n// Brand Primary: #31A062\n// Neutrals/Background: #F6F6F6 (light grey background) or #FFFFFF (white)\n// Surface/Card backgrounds: #FFFFFF\n// Text main: #1A1A1A (dark grey/black)\n// Text secondary: #828282 (medium grey)\n// Text tertiary/disabled: #BDBDBD (light grey)\n// Semantic Gain: #31A062\n// Semantic Loss/Error: #EB5757 (red)\n// Accent/Coins background or card overlay backgrounds.\n//\n// Let's fetch the actual vector icons so we can copy them!\n// On page 1:4 (04 · Media), the icons are inside frame 5:90, which is inside 5:88 (\"05 ICONS (VECTOR)\") inside 5:6 (\"Body\") inside 5:2 (\"Media Library\").\n// Wait, the icons are:\n// - Icon_Tab_Home (\"5:91\")\n// - Icon_Tab_Product_Search (\"5:95\")\n// - Icon_Tab_Transaction (\"5:99\")\n// - Icon_Tab_Account (\"5:103\")\n// - Icon_Menu (\"5:107\")\n// - Icon_Notification (\"5:111\")\n// - Icon_Back (\"5:115\")\n// - Icon_Chevron (\"5:119\")\n// - Icon_Close (\"5:123\")\n// - Icon_More (\"5:127\")\n// - Icon_Edit (\"5:131\")\n// - Icon_Upvote (\"5:135\")\n// - Icon_Contact_Info (\"5:139\")\n// - Icon_Source_of_Funding (\"5:143\")\n// - Icon_Bank_Account (\"5:147\")\n// - Icon_Document (\"5:151\")\n// - Icon_Settings (\"5:155\")\n//\n// We can find these icons in our script, and duplicate them (`.clone()`) into our frames in \"03 · Workspace\"!\n// This is fantastic and ensures perfect component reuse and brand consistency without redrawing anything.\n// Let's verify how to write a script that does this cloning.\n// Wait, when we clone a component or instance or frame, we can place it into our frames.\n// Let's test cloning an icon in a script.\n// Let's write a script that switches to the Workspace page and creates a test frame with some components, and check if it runs.\nasync function createTestFrame() {\n  const workspacePage = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === \"2003:2\");\n  if (!workspacePage) throw new Error(\"Workspace page not found\");\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(workspacePage);\n\n  // Clean up any existing children first to ensure a clean slate\n  for (const child of workspacePage.children) {\n    child.remove();\n  }\n\n  // Create a frame\n  const frame = figma.createFrame();\n  frame.name = \"Test_Frame\";\n  frame.resize(414, 932);\n  frame.x = 0;\n  frame.y = 0;\n  workspacePage.appendChild(frame);\n\n  return \"Test frame created successfully!\";\n}\n\ncreateTestFrame().then(msg => {\n  throw new Error(\"SUCCESS:\" + msg);\n}).catch(err => {\n  throw new Error(\"ERROR:\" + err.message);\n});\n","description":"Create a test frame inside Workspace page after setting it active.","fileKey":"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50079,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885502f9-7195-4d21-a73d-fafd5215030c","uuid":"1f8ccf1b-7f02-461f-999c-23201d5cea8f","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:27:56.467Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_a3abbc1fb7ad4f949792a35eb73edf93","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
