{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281130147007978358268d9d64MPh6cYl","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_41dae891151d4a72abcb0b75a42de883","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"// Oh! The children of Workspace page are empty []! Why?\n// Ah! Let's check my code in the previous tool execution:\n// \"Code executed with no return value.\"\n// It means the script ran successfully, but did it throw an error?\n// Wait, the previous script had:\n// `createTestFrame().then(msg => { throw new Error(\"SUCCESS:\" + msg); }).catch(...)`\n// But wait! If we do `throw new Error(...)` inside a `.then()` handler, does the plugin sandbox catch and print it, or does it ignore unhandled promise rejections or async throws if they are not at the top level?\n// Ah! In some JS environments, an error thrown asynchronously inside a promise handler that is NOT awaited at the top level might be swallowed or result in an unhandled promise rejection that doesn't propagate as a standard execution error!\n// That explains it! We MUST `await` our async functions directly at the top level of the script, rather than using `.then(...)` without awaiting!\n// Let's write the code like this:\n// ```javascript\n// async function run() {\n//   ...\n// }\n// run().catch(err => { ... }); // wait, still uses a promise\n// ```\n// It is much safer to write:\n// ```javascript\n// (async () => {\n//   try {\n//     const result = await createTestFrame();\n//     // Create some indicator or set a property, or just do console.log, or throw directly in the main thread:\n//     // wait, throwing inside an IIFE that is awaited is good.\n//   } catch(e) {\n//     ...\n//   }\n// })();\n// ```\n// Even better, write it as a flat script without putting it inside an async function if we don't need to, or if we use async/await, we can write:\n// `await createTestFrame();` at the top level! Yes! The Figma use_figma tool runs code in an async-supported context, so we can use top-level `await`!\n// Let's test top-level `await` to set the page and create a frame.\nasync function createTestFrame() {\n  const workspacePage = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === \"2003:2\");\n  if (!workspacePage) throw new Error(\"Workspace page not found\");\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(workspacePage);\n\n  for (const child of workspacePage.children) {\n    child.remove();\n  }\n\n  const frame = figma.createFrame();\n  frame.name = \"Test_Frame\";\n  frame.resize(414, 932);\n  frame.x = 0;\n  frame.y = 0;\n  workspacePage.appendChild(frame);\n\n  return \"Test frame created successfully!\";\n}\n\nconst msg = await createTestFrame();\nthrow new Error(\"SUCCESS:\" + msg);\n","description":"Use top-level await to create test frame and ensure it executes correctly.","fileKey":"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52531,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885502f9-7195-4d21-a73d-fafd5215030c","uuid":"57a940c6-8ef2-4b9a-a92f-75c329e3b271","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:30:22.374Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_41dae891151d4a72abcb0b75a42de883","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
