{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281132348170329348268d9d6TaHbtFwo","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_7d31bf56a8d646519b4a4189336678b9","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"// Wait, WORKSPACE_CHILDREN is empty [] again?! Why?!\n// Ah! In Figma plugins, if a script throws an exception, are the changes rolled back?\n// Oh! Yes! In many transactional systems or plugin execution environments (like Figma's console or plugin run), if the execution throws an unhandled exception or terminates with an error, all changes made during that transaction are automatically rolled back!\n// This is a major revelation! That's why whenever we throw an error (like `throw new Error(...)`), the changes we just made are reverted, and the page is empty when we query it next!\n// Yes! To persist changes in Figma, the script MUST complete successfully WITHOUT throwing any errors!\n// This makes perfect sense! If we want to inspect or return values, we should log them to the console, or write them to a temporary node, or just let the script run successfully, and then query the state using a read-only script (which doesn't modify anything but can throw to report findings, or simply let the modified state remain).\n// Let's test this theory: we will run a script that creates the test frame and completes normally (no throw, no error). Then we will run a second script that queries the workspace page and throws to see if the frame is there.\nasync function createTestFrameNoThrow() {\n  const workspacePage = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === \"2003:2\");\n  if (!workspacePage) return \"Workspace page not found\";\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(workspacePage);\n\n  for (const child of workspacePage.children) {\n    child.remove();\n  }\n\n  const frame = figma.createFrame();\n  frame.name = \"Test_Frame\";\n  frame.resize(414, 932);\n  frame.x = 0;\n  frame.y = 0;\n  workspacePage.appendChild(frame);\n\n  console.log(\"Created successfully\");\n}\n\nawait createTestFrameNoThrow();\n// Completed normally!\n","description":"Create a frame and complete successfully without throwing, to see if changes persist.","fileKey":"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":53951,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885502f9-7195-4d21-a73d-fafd5215030c","uuid":"830c4e59-47f6-4db3-9007-4cd51f408615","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:32:41.508Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_7d31bf56a8d646519b4a4189336678b9","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
