{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-202610281151209691491558268d9d6b6yzmR2Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_3a8bd5cd956045aea04148400c8f2792","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"// Wow! The schema validation for `node.reactions` in Figma's Plugin API has some very specific requirements:\n// 1. Trigger:\n//    - For tapping, the enum value is `ON_CLICK`, not `ON_TAP`! Yes! \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'ON_CLICK' | ... received 'ON_TAP'\".\n//    - For delayed transition, the trigger is `AFTER_TIMEOUT` with property `timeout` (positive number of milliseconds), not `AFTER_DELAY` with `delay`!\n// 2. Action:\n//    - For navigating to another node, the action type is `NAVIGATE`, not `NODE`! Wait:\n//      - The validator says: \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition' at [0].actions[0]\".\n//      - It means for a navigation action, the shape should be:\n//        `{ type: \"NAVIGATE\", destinationId: targetId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: ... }` or similar. Let's check: \"Invalid literal value, expected 'URL'...\"\n//      - Wait, let's look at the action type in the error trace:\n//        \"Invalid literal value, expected \"SET_VARIABLE\"... Expected [0].actions[0].type to be one of the following, but none matched...\"\n//        Wait, let's check what the valid navigation action type is in Figma API:\n//        In the Figma Plugin API, the action is defined as:\n//        - `type: \"NODE\"` with `destinationId` is the old shape, or is it:\n//        - `type: \"NAVIGATE\", destinationId: ...`?\n//        Ah! The error trace says:\n//        \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition' at [0].actions[0]\" when type was \"NODE\".\n//        Let's look at the alternatives in the schema validation:\n//        - Is there a type called \"NODE\"? No, \"Unrecognized key(s) ...\".\n//        - Ah! In the second alternative:\n//          \"Expected [0].actions[0].transition to be one of the following, but none matched: ... easing\"\n//          Wait! If `type: \"NODE\"` was unrecognized, what is the correct action shape for a navigate reaction?\n//          Let's search or test. In Figma API, a navigation action is typically represented by:\n//          `{ type: \"NODE\", destinationId: targetId, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: null }`\n//          Wait, why did the validation say \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition' at [0].actions[0]\"?\n//          Ah! Because `type: \"NODE\"` failed other options first, then for the \"NODE\" type option:\n//          Wait, did it fail because of `transition: { type: \"DISSOLVE\", duration: 0.3 }`?\n//          Ah! Let's check the transition validator part:\n//          `Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' at [0].actions[0].transition.type`\n//          Yes! `DISSOLVE` is not a valid enum value for `transition.type` inside a navigation action! The valid types are `'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT'` or `null`!\n//          And:\n//          `Required value missing at [0].actions[0].transition.easing`\n//          Yes! We missed `easing` inside transition! If transition is not null, it must have an `easing` property: `{ type: \"EASE_IN_AND_OUT\", duration: 0.3 }` or similar!\n//          Wait, what if we set `transition: null`? That is perfectly valid and super simple! It will navigate instantly without complex transition object issues!\n//          Let's verify. Yes, instant navigation `transition: null` is fully supported and robust!\n//          And what about `AFTER_TIMEOUT` trigger? It expects `timeout` in milliseconds (e.g. `timeout: 1500`), and `type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\"`.\n//          And what about `ON_CLICK` trigger? It expects `type: \"ON_CLICK\"`.\n//          Let's verify this! Let's write a script that sets a simple reaction on Splash (`ON_CLICK` or `AFTER_TIMEOUT` with `transition: null`) and see if it passes validation.\n\nconst testCode = `\nconst workspacePage = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === \"2003:2\");\nconst f01 = workspacePage.children.find(c => c.name === \"01_Splash\");\nconst f02 = workspacePage.children.find(c => c.name === \"02_Welcome\");\nif (f01 && f02) {\n  f01.reactions = [{\n    trigger: { type: \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", timeout: 1500 },\n    actions: [{\n      type: \"NODE\",\n      destinationId: f02.id,\n      navigation: \"NAVIGATE\",\n      transition: null\n    }]\n  }];\n  throw new Error(\"VALIDATION_PASSED\");\n}\nthrow new Error(\"Frames not found\");\n`;\n\nawait figma.use_figma({\n  code: testCode,\n  description: \"Test prototype connection schema with AFTER_TIMEOUT and transition: null.\",\n  fileKey: \"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q\"\n});\n","description":"Test custom navigation transition payload structure to pass validation.","fileKey":"1Dyjg6o91wFpVkfahevN0Q"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":151391,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"885502f9-7195-4d21-a73d-fafd5215030c","uuid":"a3bec5be-5943-4fd7-a231-f55c50430788","timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:51:34.243Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_3a8bd5cd956045aea04148400c8f2792","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
